Done. All six items implemented in `app/auth.py` and `app/main.py`, verified against the challenge's validator — 9/9 checks pass (EXCELLENT).

What changed:
- **`app/auth.py:6`** — `require_api_key` now rejects a missing/invalid `X-API-Key` with HTTP 401 and returns the username on success.
- **`app/main.py`** — `GET /tasks` accepts `status` (typed as `TaskStatus` enum, so invalid values get 422), `priority`, `assigned_to` — all optional, combinable — then slices by `page`/`page_size` (defaults 1/20, both `ge=1`). `POST /tasks` is auth-protected, returns 404 for an unknown `project_id`, auto-generates the next `max(id)+1`, returns 201 with the created task. `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` and `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` are auth-protected, return 404 when missing; PUT applies only the fields sent (`exclude_unset=True`), DELETE returns 204.

One judgment call worth flagging: the scaffold's `GET /tasks` returned a bare list, so I kept that shape rather than wrapping in `{items: ...}` — the validator accepts either, and it stays consistent with `response_model=List[Task]`. If you'd rather pagination metadata (total, pages), say so and I'll switch it.
